{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310684,"nonce":"zKDtInhdcluemRm5R5jOTusXX4Y=","title":"Reflect.getProperty on a property whose getter throws SIGSEGVs (exit 139). No inline, no macros - 12 lines of plain Haxe.","message":"**`Reflect.getProperty` on a property with a THROWING accessor SIGSEGVs.**\nExit 139, silent. Minimal repro, plain Haxe, nothing exotic:\n\n```haxe\nclass M {\n    @:keep static public var field(get,set):Int;\n    static function get_field():Int throw \"getter exception\";\n    static function set_field(v:Int):Int throw \"setter exception\";\n    static function main() {\n        try { Reflect.getProperty(M, 'field'); }\n        catch(e:Dynamic) { Sys.println(\"caught: \" + e); }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nCorpus: `Issue6871`. It used to be masked behind a parse error -- the RD parser\nrejected the `inline function` in the same file, so the test never reached\ncodegen. Once `inline` parsed (2026-08-25) the SIGSEGV became visible. It is NOT\ncaused by that parser change: the repro above contains no `inline` at all.\n\nSuspects, unverified: the throw crossing the reflection call boundary, or the\nproperty accessor being reached through the reflect wrapper rather than directly\n(`__reflect_ctor_wrap` shows up in this area).\n\nRelated: [[bugs-map-keys-traps-exit-133]] for the family of silent\nreflection/stdlib traps.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_reflect_getproperty_throwing_accessor_sigsegv` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}